  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is projected at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">t</mtext><mtext>&nbsp;=&nbsp;0</mtext></math> from a point <math> <mtext>O</mtext> </math> on the ground with a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;at an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>°</mo></math>&nbsp;to the horizontal. The magnitude of the angular momentum of the particle about <math> <mtext>O</mtext> </math> at the time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">t</mtext><mtext>&nbsp;=&nbsp;</mtext><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">v</mtext><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></math>&nbsp;is close to [Take&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math>]"
  },
